{
  "_readme": "SAMPLE / DEMO DATA ONLY. Northern Ireland postcode-to-coordinate data (unit level) is published by Land & Property Services (LPS) as the 'Pointer' dataset via the NI Open Data portal (opendatani.gov.uk) under the NI Open Government Licence. It is not bundled with ONSPD/Code-Point Open in the same way GB data is, which is why it needs handling separately (see README). This file covers all ~80 real NI postcode districts (outward codes); each centroid is the geometric (area-weighted) centroid of that district's own boundary polygon in data/postcode-boundaries/output/district/, not a generic town-level geocode — this keeps every district distinct even where several share one post town (e.g. BT19/BT20 both 'Bangor'). Still DISTRICT-level, not unit-level — replace src/postcode.js's NI provider with a loader for the real Pointer CSV for production/unit-level accuracy.",
